Here is the input problem:
  Axiom 1 (eqNat_1): eqNat(zero, zero) = true.
  Axiom 2 (eqNat_2): eqNat(zero, suc(X)) = false.
  Axiom 3 (eqNat_3): eqNat(suc(X), zero) = false.
  Axiom 4 (eqNat_4): eqNat(suc(X), suc(Y)) = eqNat(X, Y).
  Axiom 5 (app_fn_id_1): app(fn_id, X) = X.
  Axiom 6 (app_fn_const_1): app(fn_const(X), Y) = X.
  Axiom 7 (app_fn_case_Nat_1): app(fn_case_Nat(X, Y), zero) = X.
  Axiom 8 (app_fn_case_Nat_2): app(fn_case_Nat(X, Y), suc(Z)) = app(Y, Z).
  Axiom 9 (prop_fnSuc_1): prop_fnSuc(X, Y) = eqNat(app(X, suc(Y)), suc(app(X, Y))).
  Axiom 10 (reflexivity): equals(X, X) = true.
  Axiom 11 (prop_fnSuc): equals(prop_fnSuc(X, Y), false) = false.
  Goal 1 (true_equals_false): true = false.

1. eqNat(zero, zero) -> true
2. eqNat(zero, suc(X)) -> false
3. eqNat(suc(X), zero) -> false
4. eqNat(suc(X), suc(Y)) -> eqNat(X, Y)
5. app(fn_id, X) -> X
6. app(fn_const(X), Y) -> X
7. app(fn_case_Nat(X, Y), zero) -> X
8. app(fn_case_Nat(X, Y), suc(Z)) -> app(Y, Z)
9. eqNat(app(X, suc(Y)), suc(app(X, Y))) -> prop_fnSuc(X, Y)
10. equals(X, X) -> true
11. equals(prop_fnSuc(X, Y), false) -> false
12. eqNat(X, X) -> prop_fnSuc(fn_id, X)
13. prop_fnSuc(fn_id, zero) -> true
14. equals(true, false) -> false
15. prop_fnSuc(fn_const(X), ?) = eqNat(X, suc(X))
16. prop_fnSuc(fn_const(X), Y) ~> prop_fnSuc(fn_const(X), ?)
17. prop_fnSuc(fn_id, suc(X)) -> prop_fnSuc(fn_id, X)
18. prop_fnSuc(fn_case_Nat(X, Y), suc(Z)) -> prop_fnSuc(Y, Z)
19. eqNat(X, suc(X)) = prop_fnSuc(fn_const(suc(X)), ?)
20. equals(eqNat(X, suc(X)), false) -> false
21. false -> true

The conjecture is true! Here is a proof.

Axiom 1 (eqNat_2): eqNat(zero, suc(X)) = false.
Axiom 2 (app_fn_const_1): app(fn_const(X), Y) = X.
Axiom 3 (prop_fnSuc_1): prop_fnSuc(X, Y) = eqNat(app(X, suc(Y)), suc(app(X, Y))).

Goal 1 (prop_fnSuc): prop_fnSuc(X, Y) = false.
The goal is true when:
  X = fn_const(zero)
  Y = X

Proof:
  prop_fnSuc(fn_const(zero), X)
= { by axiom 3 (prop_fnSuc_1) }
  eqNat(app(fn_const(zero), suc(X)), suc(app(fn_const(zero), X)))
= { by axiom 2 (app_fn_const_1) }
  eqNat(zero, suc(app(fn_const(zero), X)))
= { by axiom 2 (app_fn_const_1) }
  eqNat(zero, suc(zero))
= { by axiom 1 (eqNat_2) }
  false

RESULT: Theorem (the conjecture is true).
